# DOCUMENTATION-BASED lines — composed, NOT captured: a large server's gateway had sent none of these yet (2026-10-08, the first
# hours with «Blocked Traffic Only»). Built from the shapes in the router SOC concept 1.1 (the Wazuh-Unifi decoders,
# Graylog's content pack, Security Onion's UniFi guide) and the router SOC neighbours notes 5 (the netfilter prefix as
# FireSight's and CrowdSec's regexes read it: [ZONE-ACTION-RULEID] / [ZONE-RULEID-ACTION]), in the header shape of the real
# 10.6.106 lines (unifi-10.6.106-real.log: «CEF: 0|», the header's local time, UNIFIutcTime). ASSUMED and to be checked
# against a captured line: the event ids and names of Wired Client Connected, Threat Detected and Blocked, Admin Made
# Config Changes, VPN Client Connected, Device Updated, WAN Failover; the VPN fields (UNIFIvpnUser, UNIFIvpnType); the
# zone names in the netfilter prefixes. Addresses: 192.0.2.20 = this server, 192.0.2.x the LAN, 203.0.113.x the internet.
# Lines starting with # are this header (the tests leave them out).
